---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/lib/site';

const canonical = `${SITE.url}/privacy`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How mlsystems.dev handles data — analytics, cookies, and the in-browser writing tool. Plain language."
  canonical={canonical}
>
  <div class="container privacy-page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Policy</div>
      <h1 class="page-h1">Privacy.</h1>
      <p class="page-lede">Last updated July 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="article-body">
      <p>
        This is a plain-language summary of how {SITE.name} handles your data. The short version: we collect
        as little as possible, we don't sell anything, and there are no user accounts.
      </p>

      <h2>No accounts, no logins</h2>
      <p>
        You can read everything without signing in. The in-browser writing tool at <code
          >/write</code
        > runs entirely in your browser — what you type stays on your device, and nothing is sent to us
        until you choose to download it and submit it by pull request, issue, or email.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics to understand aggregate traffic — which pages are read, roughly
        where visitors come from, and what devices they use. It's loaded through Google's Consent
        Mode, so analytics cookies are only set after you accept them. We use this to improve the
        site, not to identify you personally, and we never sell or share this data.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We store your consent choice so we don't ask on every visit. Analytics cookies are only set
        if you accept. You can clear these at any time through your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served as static files by our host, and fonts are self-hosted (no third-party
        font requests). If comments or discussions are enabled, they are powered by GitHub and
        subject to <a href="https://github.com/site/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
          >GitHub's privacy policy</a
        >. Google Analytics is subject to <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Your author profile</h2>
      <p>
        If you contribute an article, the author details you choose to share — name, bio, and any
        links — are published on your profile page. Share only what you want public; anything you
        leave out simply won't appear.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, or want your data or a contribution removed? Email <a
          href={`mailto:${SITE.pitchEmail}`}>{SITE.pitchEmail}</a
        >.
      </p>

      <p>
        We may update this page as the site changes. Material changes will be reflected in the date
        above.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    padding-top: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 80px;
  }
  .page-head {
    padding: 20px 0 12px;
  }
  .page-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(40px, 7vw, 72px);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    line-height: 1.02;
    margin: 6px 0 0;
  }
  .page-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .privacy-page .article-body {
    max-width: 680px;
  }
</style>
